            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>At the time of the inspection we notice some air leakage on the following house components:

-Receptacles

-Attic hatch

-Doors (basement door)

The addition of weather strippings might help to increase the air tightness of the items listed above. 

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>The actual insulation level of your attic is R-46, we recommend the addition of insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. 

The addition of insulation will increase your capacity to retain heat into the living space and reduce heat loss during winter. In the summertime, the addition of insulation will slow down the migration of heat from the attic to the upper floor. The upgraded attic insulation suggested is based on the addition of 2 layers of 6??????????????????  of Fiberglass batt insulation (pink one).

</ceilings>
                <VentilationSystem>The natural ventilation airflow is not enough to ensure good air quality and proper ventilation. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified. </VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
